Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.9.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.9.0 fixes the one defect reported on device in 0.8.0 (archive #8): the floating window finally rendered correctly and scaled correctly with no safe mode, but as soon as the user switched from the home screen to another app (Settings), the hosted content went black. The log shows the exact chain within one hosting round: P6 foreground=1 contentState=2 layerManager.layers=2 hostContainer.hostedLayers=2 (good), then P6+20s foreground=0 contentState=0 layerManager.layers=0 hostedLayers=0 (black). Root cause: the P0 step that forces the scene renderable (foreground=YES / level=1) is a ONE-SHOT. Whenever the foreground app changes, SpringBoard recomputes the target app's scene settings, writes foreground=NO back (and is very likely to switch idleModeEnabled on and add deactivationReasons), the app's layer manager drops all of its layers, and the _UIScenePresentationView is left hosting nothing, which draws black. 0.9.0 therefore adds a scene keep-alive: after a successful mount a repeating timer (default every 1000 ms) re-asserts foreground=YES, level=1, idleModeEnabled=NO and deactivationReasons=0, re-syncs scene.frame to the content-area size, and re-issues presenter activate if isHosting dropped. Both setters were confirmed present on this device by the archive #8 capability report (UIMutableApplicationSceneSettings -setDeactivationReasons: and -setIdleModeEnabled:). The keep-alive logs one line only when the state signature actually changes (plus one heartbeat every 20 ticks), so the log stays small enough to send back. It stops on window close, on target change, and when the scene becomes invalid, and it never touches another app's scene once the float is gone. Still no hooks are installed anywhere: the fix uses only updateSettingsWithBlock:, the same non-invasive call already proven to make the picture appear in 0.7.0, just held down continuously instead of fired once. Config, all defaults can be overridden in /var/mobile/MultiFloat.plist: hostRoute 3 (3 = adopt the existing scene, 4 = build our own, now guarded), hostSceneFrame true, resizesHosted true, forceForeground true, keepAlive true, keepAliveMs 1000, keepAliveIdle true (turn it off for a clean A/B test of whether idleModeEnabled alone is the culprit), allowRouteB false, hostStep 6. Config structure version cfgVersion=9, migrated once on first launch. DISABLED BY DEFAULT for real hosting: needs enabled=true AND hostEnabled=true. Crash-guard marker still makes a crash loop impossible. Log: /var/mobile/MultiFloat.log
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
